# Every version docs/project-context.md claims, bound to the manifest entry that owns it.
#
# That page exists to tell an agent what its training data gets wrong about THIS stack, and it is read
# far more widely than its history suggests: 60 of the 90 installed skills declare it in
# `persistent_facts`, so it is loaded as foundational context at the start of an agent session rather
# than consulted on demand. A stale line there is not documentation rot — it is a false premise handed
# to the agent before it reads any code, asserted with exactly the confidence of a true one.
#
# The page states normative rules too, and no cheap check can falsify those. The versions are the part
# that can be, so they are the part gated here. Measured over the page's own history: ten drifted
# claims, ALL of them prose, against ZERO wrong version numbers — so a green here is silent about the
# direction that has actually drifted.
#
# Format:  <manifest> :: <dotted path> => <token exactly as written on the page>
#          unbound    :: <why nothing can own it> => <token exactly as written on the page>
#
# The token carries its product name on purpose. Binding the bare number would make the staleness
# direction a tautology — "4" appears in any page of prose — so the check would pass over a page that no
# longer mentions Behat at all. The version is the token's last whitespace-separated word.
#
# The gate (make php.lint.project-context) checks three things:
#   - the manifest still starts with the token's version, so a bump that skips the page fails;
#   - the token still appears verbatim on the page, so rewording a cell without touching this file
#     fails rather than leaving a line guarding a claim nobody makes any more;
#   - every version the page's tables claim is covered by a line here, so a claim added to the page
#     with no entry fails instead of passing in silence.
#
# "Starts with" is a floor, and only a constraint that HAS a floor is read: `^`, `~`, `>=`, `=`, a bare
# version and a wildcard. `<`, `>`, `!=` and any union are refused rather than guessed at — the earlier
# spelling stripped those characters as a charlist, which inverted them, and `<2.0` satisfied the claim
# "2.0" while `^24.15.0 || >=26.0.0` satisfied "24" on a container running 26.
#
# The universe is the PAGE's claims, not the manifests' keys: the second column of each table row, on
# the word carrying the number. 33 claims over the page at 406 lines, no false positives. A claim whose
# version-bearing word is a bare noun ("bundle 4.0") is unreadable to a reviewer as well as to the
# extractor — rename it on the page rather than teaching the gate to guess.
#
# What a green does NOT prove:
#   - Nothing about the third column of those tables. It is prose, it is where every measured drift
#     landed, and no cheap check can falsify it — reading the code is the only control. Nor about any
#     prose outside the tables, which is most of the page.
#   - Nothing about an `unbound` line beyond the fact that somebody wrote a reason. The reason is not
#     checked against anything; it is a statement made where a reviewer will see it, not a proof.
#   - Nothing about a version stated in the page's PROSE rather than in a table cell — the extraction
#     reads table rows only, and a claim moved into a paragraph leaves the universe silently.
#   - Nothing about anything pinned by digest rather than by manifest — Node and the base images.
#   - A dotted path cannot address a manifest key that itself contains a dot. None does today.

